---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import UpdatedBadge from '../../components/content/UpdatedBadge.astro';

const today = '2026-06-13T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor is a free browser-based tool that reduces image file sizes without uploading anything to a server. You drag and drop your image, adjust the quality slider, and download a smaller version instantly. It supports JPEG, PNG, and WebP formats.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the image compressor work?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor uses your browser\'s built-in Canvas API to re-encode images at a lower quality setting. When you upload an image, the browser draws it onto an invisible canvas and exports it with your chosen quality level and format. Everything happens locally on your computer. No file ever leaves your device.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the image compressor free to use?',
    a: 'Yes, the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor is completely free with no usage limits, no watermarks, and no signup required. You can compress as many images as you want, as large as you want, directly in your browser.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What image formats does the compressor support?',
    a: 'You can upload JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP, and WebP images. The output format can be set to JPEG, PNG, or WebP. WebP typically produces the smallest file sizes with the best visual quality, making it the recommended format for web use in 2026.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will image compression reduce visual quality?',
    a: 'Lossy compression like JPEG and WebP removes some image data to reduce file size. At quality settings of 70 to 85 percent, the visual difference is usually invisible to the human eye while cutting file size by 40 to 80 percent. PNG uses lossless compression, so quality stays perfect but file size reductions are smaller, typically 10 to 30 percent.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the maximum file size I can compress?',
    a: 'There is no file size limit. The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor handles everything from small thumbnails to massive high-resolution photographs. Best Answer Hub was built specifically because most free image compressors cap users at 5 MB or enforce daily quotas. The goal is a free tool with no artificial limits. For the fastest results, any image will process quickly on a modern device.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much can I compress an image?',
    a: 'Typical compression results vary by format. JPEG and WebP images can usually be reduced by 50 to 80 percent at quality 75 without visible quality loss. PNG images compress by 10 to 30 percent because PNG is already lossless. Photos with lots of detail compress more than simple graphics with flat colors.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my data safe when using this compressor?',
    a: 'Yes, completely. The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor is a client-side tool, meaning every pixel is processed inside your own browser. No image data is uploaded to any server, cloud storage, or third-party service. Even if you disconnect from the internet after loading the page, the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor continues to work.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between lossy and lossless compression?',
    a: 'Lossy compression removes image data permanently to achieve smaller files. JPEG and WebP are lossy formats. They are ideal for photographs where small file size matters more than pixel-perfect accuracy. Lossless compression preserves every pixel exactly. PNG is lossless. It is best for graphics, screenshots, logos, and images with text where sharp edges must stay crisp.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I compress images for web use?',
    a: 'Yes, and that is exactly what the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor is designed for. Web-optimized images load faster, rank better in Google PageSpeed Insights, and improve user experience. For websites in 2026, the recommended workflow is: compress to WebP at 75 to 80 percent quality, keep the width under 2,000 pixels, and use the compressed file directly on your site.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do I need to compress images for my website?',
    a: 'Large images are the number one cause of slow websites. A single uncompressed 5-megabyte photo can delay page load by several seconds on mobile connections. Google uses page speed as a ranking factor, and users abandon sites that take more than three seconds to load. Compressing images typically improves load times by 50 to 70 percent with zero visible quality loss.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I compress images for faster page speed?',
    a: 'Follow the 2026 best practice workflow: upload your image to the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor, select WebP as the output format, set quality to 75 or 80 percent, and resize the longest edge to 1,600 to 2,000 pixels for content images or 800 to 1,200 pixels for thumbnails. Download the compressed file and replace the original on your website. Test the result with Google PageSpeed Insights.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the best image format for websites in 2026?',
    a: 'WebP is the best overall format for websites in 2026. It produces files 25 to 35 percent smaller than JPEG at the same visual quality and supports transparency like PNG. All modern browsers including Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge support WebP. For maximum compatibility with very old browsers, provide a JPEG fallback. Use PNG only when you need perfect transparency with zero quality loss.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I compress multiple images at once?',
    a: 'Currently, the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor processes one image at a time. For batch compression, you can process images sequentially by uploading, compressing, and downloading each one. Each compression takes under two seconds on a modern computer. For bulk workflow, compress all images before uploading them to your website or content management system.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does compressing an image remove EXIF data and GPS location information?',
    a: 'Yes. When you compress an image using the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor, the Canvas API re-encodes the image from scratch as a brand-new file. This re-encoding process does not carry over EXIF metadata, including GPS coordinates, camera model, date taken, lens information, and other embedded tags. The output file contains only pixel data and basic format headers. This is an important privacy benefit: a compressed image shared online will not expose the location where the photo was taken or your device details. If you need to preserve EXIF data for professional photography or archival workflows, always keep your original uncompressed file before compressing.',
  },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Free Image Compressor — Reduce JPEG, PNG & WebP (2026)',
  description: 'Compress images free online. Reduce JPEG, PNG, and WebP file sizes 50-80% with no visible quality loss. No uploads — works in your browser.',
  url: '/tools/image-compressor/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: today,
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Tools', url: '/tools/' },
    { name: 'Image Compressor', url: '/tools/image-compressor/' },
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-10 pb-6 md:pt-14 md:pb-8">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="mb-5"><UpdatedBadge date={seo.dateModified} /></div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-5">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-bae-primary animate-pulse-dot"></span>
            Free Tool · No Upload to Servers
          </div>
          <a href="/tools/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink bg-white border border-bae-border px-3.5 py-2 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary hover:text-bae-primary transition-colors no-underline shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
            ← All Tools
          </a>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-4">
          Image Compressor:<br/>
          <em class="italic text-bae-primary">Shrink JPEG &amp; WebP by 50–80%</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-bae-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Compress JPEG, PNG and WebP images instantly in your browser. No uploads, no watermarks, no signup. Perfect for websites, social media, and email.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Compressor Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="Image compressor">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <!-- Drop Zone -->
        <div id="drop-zone" class="border-2 border-dashed border-bae-border rounded-bae p-8 md:p-12 text-center bg-bae-card hover:border-bae-primary hover:bg-bae-primary-soft/30 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary mx-auto mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16l4.586-4.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L16 16m-2-2l1.586-1.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L20 14m-6-6h.01M6 20h12a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-1">Drag & drop an image here</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted">or click to browse (JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP)</p>
          <input type="file" id="file-input" class="hidden" accept="image/*" />
        </div>

        <!-- Size Warning -->
        <div id="size-warning" class="hidden mt-4 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-bae p-3 flex items-start gap-2">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-2.5L13.732 4c-.77-.833-1.964-.833-2.732 0L4.082 16.5c-.77.833.192 2.5 1.732 2.5z"/></svg>
          <p class="text-xs text-amber-700">This image is very large (<strong id="warn-size"></strong>). Processing may take longer on older devices and your browser may become temporarily unresponsive.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Controls -->
        <div id="controls" class="hidden mt-6 bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Output Format</label>
              <select id="format-select" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                <option value="image/jpeg">JPEG (smallest)</option>
                <option value="image/webp">WebP (recommended)</option>
                <option value="image/png">PNG (lossless)</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Max Width (px)</label>
              <select id="width-select" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                <option value="0">Original size</option>
                <option value="3840">4K (3840px)</option>
                <option value="1920" selected>Full HD (1920px)</option>
                <option value="1280">HD (1280px)</option>
                <option value="800">Medium (800px)</option>
                <option value="400">Thumbnail (400px)</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mb-4">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-1.5">
              <label class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted">Quality</label>
              <span id="quality-value" class="text-xs font-bold text-bae-primary">75%</span>
            </div>
            <input type="range" id="quality-slider" min="10" max="100" value="75" class="w-full h-2 bg-bae-bg rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-bae-primary" />
            <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] text-bae-muted mt-1">
              <span>Smaller file</span>
              <span>Better quality</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <button id="compress-btn" class="w-full bg-bae-ink text-white font-semibold text-sm py-3 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors">
            Compress Image
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- Result -->
        <div id="result" class="hidden mt-6">
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-bae-ink">Compression Result</h3>
              <span id="savings-badge" class="text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600 border border-emerald-100">0% smaller</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
              <div class="bg-bae-bg rounded-bae-sm p-4 text-center">
                <p class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Original</p>
                <p id="original-size" class="text-lg font-bold text-bae-ink">—</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft rounded-bae-sm p-4 text-center">
                <p class="text-[11px] text-bae-primary uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Compressed</p>
                <p id="compressed-size" class="text-lg font-bold text-bae-primary">—</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-bae-sm overflow-hidden border border-bae-border mb-4">
              <img id="preview-img" class="w-full h-auto max-h-[400px] object-contain bg-bae-bg" alt="Compressed preview" />
            </div>
            <a id="download-btn" href="#" download class="block w-full text-center bg-bae-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm py-3 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-accent transition-colors no-underline">
              Download Compressed Image
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">How the image compressor works</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">1</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Upload your image</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Drag and drop or click to select any JPEG, PNG, GIF, or WebP file. The image stays on your device. Nothing is uploaded to a server.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">2</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Set quality & format</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Choose JPEG for smallest files, WebP for best web performance, or PNG for lossless quality. Adjust the quality slider to balance size and clarity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">3</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Download & use</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Click Compress, preview the result, and download the optimized image. Use it on your website, social media, or email campaigns instantly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Format Comparison -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-2">Format comparison</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-6">Which format should you choose for your use case?</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-bae border border-bae-border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-bae-bg border-b border-bae-border">
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Format</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Best For</th>
              <th class="text-right px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Typical Reduction</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Transparency</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-bae-border-light">
            <tr class="bg-bae-card hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-bae-ink">WebP</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">Websites & apps</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-bae-muted">60–85%</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-bae-card hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-bae-ink">JPEG</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">Photography</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-bae-muted">50–80%</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">No</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-bae-card hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-bae-ink">PNG</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">Logos & screenshots</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-bae-muted">10–30%</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bae-muted">Yes (lossless)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border" id="faq">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 max-w-4xl">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">{item.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who uses this tool -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">Who reaches for this tool</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">BLOG POSTS</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Content Creator: blog post images</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">4MB → 200KB</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">I used to upload 4 MB photos straight to WordPress and wonder why my site was slow. Now I run every image through the Best Answer Hub Image Compressor first (WebP at 80%) and my PageSpeed score jumped from 54 to 91.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">CLIENT DELIVERY</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Freelance Designer: client file delivery</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">WebP • 30s</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Clients send me 20 MB hero images and expect me to 'sort out the web version'. The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor lets me compress, convert to WebP, and send back a file that actually works on their site, in under 30 seconds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">PRODUCT PHOTOS</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">E-commerce Owner: product photos</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">50–80% smaller</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Product photography files are enormous. Before I upload anything to Shopify I compress every image here. Page load times improved noticeably and my conversion rate went up. Google PageSpeed was flagging images as the #1 issue.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">PRIVACY SHARING</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Privacy-Conscious User: sharing photos</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">EXIF stripped</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">I did not realise my phone photos had GPS coordinates embedded in them. The Best Answer Hub Image Compressor strips EXIF data during re-encoding, so I can share compressed images without accidentally revealing where I live or work.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-4">Scenarios are illustrative examples based on common use cases. Results vary by specific situation and requirements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Related Tools CTA -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 rounded-bae p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Explore more free tools</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">Also try <a href="/tools/ai-cost-calculator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">AI Cost Calculator</a>, <a href="/tools/pdf-to-word-converter/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">PDF to Word</a>, <a href="/tools/qr-code-generator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">QR Code</a>, <a href="/tools/password-generator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Password Generator</a>, <a href="/tools/website-speed-test/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Speed Test</a>, <a href="/tools/seo-score-checker/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">SEO Checker</a>, <a href="/tools/invoice-generator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Invoice Generator</a>, <a href="/tools/broken-link-checker/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Broken Link Checker</a>, and <a href="/developer-toolbox/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Developer Toolbox</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/tools/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-ink text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm font-semibold text-sm no-underline hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors shrink-0">
          Browse all tools →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      const dropZone = document.getElementById('drop-zone');
      const fileInput = document.getElementById('file-input');
      const controls = document.getElementById('controls');
      const result = document.getElementById('result');
      const compressBtn = document.getElementById('compress-btn');
      const formatSelect = document.getElementById('format-select');
      const widthSelect = document.getElementById('width-select');
      const qualitySlider = document.getElementById('quality-slider');
      const qualityValue = document.getElementById('quality-value');
      const originalSize = document.getElementById('original-size');
      const compressedSize = document.getElementById('compressed-size');
      const savingsBadge = document.getElementById('savings-badge');
      const previewImg = document.getElementById('preview-img');
      const downloadBtn = document.getElementById('download-btn');

      let currentFile = null;
      let originalDataUrl = null;
      let currentObjUrl = null;

      function formatBytes(bytes) {
        if (bytes === 0) return '0 B';
        const k = 1024;
        const sizes = ['B', 'KB', 'MB', 'GB', 'TB'];
        const i = Math.floor(Math.log(bytes) / Math.log(k));
        return parseFloat((bytes / Math.pow(k, i)).toFixed(2)) + ' ' + sizes[i];
      }

      const sizeWarning = document.getElementById('size-warning');
      const warnSize = document.getElementById('warn-size');

      function validateFile(file, exts, mimePrefix) {
        const nameOk = exts.some(e => file.name.toLowerCase().endsWith(e));
        const mimeOk = file.type.startsWith(mimePrefix);
        return nameOk && mimeOk;
      }

      const MAX_FILE_SIZE = 20 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
      function handleFile(file) {
        if (!file || !validateFile(file, ['.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png', '.gif', '.webp', '.bmp'], 'image/')) return;
        if (file.size > MAX_FILE_SIZE) {
          alert('File too large. Maximum size is 20 GB.');
          return;
        }
        if (currentObjUrl) { URL.revokeObjectURL(currentObjUrl); currentObjUrl = null; }
        currentFile = file;
        if (file.size > 100 * 1024 * 1024) {
          warnSize.textContent = formatBytes(file.size);
          sizeWarning.classList.remove('hidden');
        } else {
          sizeWarning.classList.add('hidden');
        }
        const reader = new FileReader();
        reader.onload = function(e) {
          originalDataUrl = e.target.result;
          controls.classList.remove('hidden');
          result.classList.add('hidden');
          originalSize.textContent = formatBytes(file.size);
        };
        reader.readAsDataURL(file);
      }

      dropZone.addEventListener('click', () => fileInput.click());
      dropZone.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); dropZone.classList.add('border-bae-primary', 'bg-bae-primary-soft/50'); });
      dropZone.addEventListener('dragleave', () => { dropZone.classList.remove('border-bae-primary', 'bg-bae-primary-soft/50'); });
      dropZone.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        dropZone.classList.remove('border-bae-primary', 'bg-bae-primary-soft/50');
        if (e.dataTransfer.files.length) handleFile(e.dataTransfer.files[0]);
      });
      fileInput.addEventListener('change', (e) => { if (e.target.files.length) handleFile(e.target.files[0]); });

      qualitySlider.addEventListener('input', () => {
        qualityValue.textContent = qualitySlider.value + '%';
      });

      compressBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!originalDataUrl) return;

        const img = new Image();
        img.onload = function() {
          const maxWidth = parseInt(widthSelect.value, 10);
          let w = img.width;
          let h = img.height;

          if (maxWidth > 0 && w > maxWidth) {
            h = Math.round(h * (maxWidth / w));
            w = maxWidth;
          }

          const MAX_CANVAS_DIM = 8192;
          if (w > MAX_CANVAS_DIM || h > MAX_CANVAS_DIM) {
            const scale = Math.min(MAX_CANVAS_DIM / w, MAX_CANVAS_DIM / h);
            w = Math.round(w * scale);
            h = Math.round(h * scale);
          }

          const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
          canvas.width = w;
          canvas.height = h;
          const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
          ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, w, h);

          const mime = formatSelect.value;
          const quality = parseInt(qualitySlider.value, 10) / 100;
          const outputType = mime === 'image/png' ? 'image/png' : mime;
          const outputQuality = mime === 'image/png' ? undefined : quality;

          canvas.toBlob(function(blob) {
            if (!blob) {
              alert('Compression failed. Your browser could not encode this image in the selected format. Try a different output format such as JPEG.');
              return;
            }
            if (currentObjUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(currentObjUrl);
            const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            currentObjUrl = url;
            previewImg.src = url;
            compressedSize.textContent = formatBytes(blob.size);

            const savings = Math.round((1 - blob.size / currentFile.size) * 100);
            if (savings > 0) {
              savingsBadge.textContent = savings + '% smaller';
              savingsBadge.className = 'text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600 border border-emerald-100';
            } else {
              savingsBadge.textContent = 'Same size';
              savingsBadge.className = 'text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 border border-amber-100';
            }

            const ext = outputType.split('/')[1];
            const name = currentFile.name.replace(/\.[^/.]+$/, '') + '-compressed.' + ext;
            downloadBtn.href = url;
            downloadBtn.download = name;

            result.classList.remove('hidden');
            result.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
          }, outputType, outputQuality);
        };
        img.src = originalDataUrl;
      });
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
